---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { business } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Learn how M&H Construction handles information submitted through this website and how to contact us about your information.">
  <section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">M&amp;H CONSTRUCTION</p><h1>Privacy<br /><em>policy.</em></h1><p class="intro-text">This policy explains how M&amp;H Construction handles information collected through this website and when you contact us.</p><p>Last updated: November 7, 2026</p></section>
  <article class="container legal-copy">
    <h2>Information you provide</h2>
    <p>When you contact us, you may provide your name, email address, phone number, project type and description, city, preferred timing, approximate budget, and other details you choose to share. The contact form requires your name, project type, project description, and at least one way to reply: an email address or phone number. Planning details are optional.</p>
    <p>Please do not include sensitive information, such as payment details, government identification numbers, medical information, or your exact home address, in your initial inquiry.</p>
    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <p>We use the information you provide to respond to your inquiry, discuss and evaluate your project, communicate with you, and maintain records related to those conversations and our business. If you call or email us directly, we use the information you share for the same purposes.</p>
    <h2>Service providers and sharing</h2>
    <p>Our contact form sends your information to Formspree, which processes and stores submissions and can send them to our email account. Our email provider processes messages we receive and send. The company hosting the website and its service providers may process technical information to operate, secure, and maintain the site. These providers handle information according to their own terms and privacy policies. You can read <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree’s privacy policy</a> for more information.</p>
    <p>We may also disclose information when required by law or when reasonably necessary to protect our rights, safety, or business.</p>
    <h2>Website data and cookies</h2>
    <p>The website itself does not currently include analytics, advertising pixels, or tracking cookies. Hosting and other service providers may collect technical information, such as IP address, browser details, requested pages, and access times, in server or security logs. Their practices depend on how those services are configured.</p>
    <h2>Retention and security</h2>
    <p>Form submissions may be stored in Formspree and in our email and business records. How long information is kept depends on the service’s settings and the needs of the inquiry, project, recordkeeping, and applicable law. Copies may remain in backups or service-provider systems after a deletion request.</p>
    <p>We use service providers to process and store information, but no method of transmission or storage can be guaranteed completely secure. Please avoid sending sensitive information through the form or ordinary email.</p>
    <h2>Your requests and questions</h2>
    <p>To ask about, correct, or request deletion of information you have provided, contact us at <a href={business.emailHref}>{business.email}</a> or <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>. We may need to verify your identity and may retain information where needed for legitimate business purposes or as required or permitted by law. Depending on where you live and applicable law, you may have additional rights concerning your personal information.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as our website or practices change. The date at the top reflects the most recent update.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
